cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these validation cases, please cite them as below and also cite the original source of each case (see the source field in cases/*.json)."
title: "Acribi calculator validation cases"
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Acribi"
    website: "https://acribi.com"
    email: "hello@acribi.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/acribi/calculator-validation"
url: "https://acribi.com"
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-29"
abstract: >-
  Machine-readable test cases for metrology calculators (TUR and measurement
  decision risk, guard banding, GUM uncertainty budgets with Welch-Satterthwaite,
  gauge R&R, gravimetric pipette calibration, calibration intervals, pressure
  gauges, scales and balances, boiling point of water). Each case traces to a
  worked example in a published source and gives inputs, expected outputs with
  units and tolerances, and the exact citation. Includes a small reference
  runner in JavaScript for Node.js.
keywords:
  - metrology
  - calibration
  - measurement uncertainty
  - GUM
  - test uncertainty ratio
  - decision rules
  - guard banding
  - gauge R&R
  - validation
